    <div id="hardware-overview" class="content-card">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p class="hardware-lede">The Echo Yeast temperature-controlled incubation and optical readout module.</p>
      <p>This page documents the device we designed and built for the PAGER-Yeast biosensor: a temperature-controlled incubation and optical readout module that keeps the engineered yeast at 30 °C, excites the green fluorescent protein they express at 485 nm, and reads the 528 nm emission back as an electrical signal.</p>
      <p>The sampling cup is also the culture cup and the detection cell.</p>
      <p>Influenza arrives every year, and the way we watch for it is arranged almost entirely around people: someone develops a fever or a cough, a swab is taken, the sample goes to a laboratory, and a result comes back later. There is nothing wrong with that chain — it simply starts a little too late. By the time the result exists, the virus may already have made its way through classrooms, wards and waiting halls.</p>
      <p>This module is our answer to the half of that chain that never reaches a laboratory in time. It is designed to sit next to a wet-cyclone sampler, hold the yeast that does the sensing, and turn their fluorescence into a reading that does not have to travel.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why the device exists</strong> — <a href="#hardware-problem">Problem Statement</a> and <a href="#hardware-worth">What the Hardware Is Worth</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>What it is made of</strong> — <a href="#hardware-architecture">Optical &amp; Electronic Architecture</a>, <a href="#hardware-specifications">Current Specifications</a> and <a href="#hardware-bom">Bill of Materials</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>How it was built and how it changed</strong> — <a href="#hardware-iterations">Design Iterations</a> and the date-by-date <a href="#hardware-log">Hardware Log</a> with 27 figures.</li>
        <li><strong>How far it will be taken</strong> — <a href="#hardware-instrument">The Complete Instrument</a> and <a href="#hardware-test-plan">Test Plan</a>.</li>
      </ul>
