    <div id="hardware-architecture" class="content-card">
      <h2>Optical and Electronic Architecture</h2>

      <h3 id="hardware-optics">Optical path</h3>
      <p class="hardware-chain">485 nm LED → focusing lens → 485 nm narrow-band filter → vessel (cuvette / collection cup) → 528 nm narrow-band filter → focusing lens → BPW34 photodiode → OPA350 transimpedance amplifier → ADS1115 (16-bit, I²C).</p>

      <h3 id="hardware-thermal">Temperature control</h3>
      <p class="hardware-chain">PT100 (3-wire) → MAX31865 (16-bit, SPI) → PID loop on the microcontroller → IRF520 (PWM) → PI heating film, with a KSD9700 (60 °C) in series with the heater as hardware-level protection.</p>

      <h3 id="hardware-power">Power</h3>
      <p class="hardware-chain">24 V adapter → LM2596 → 12 V (heating film, fan) and 5 V (logic). Power and signal wiring are routed separately so that switching noise does not couple into the microampere-level photocurrent.</p>
    </div>

